{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779397225,"nonce":"kt8jd4gxvocCzOspF7hvx4YBaLw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDPrQyA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4512731336"},"message":"## Correction (2026-05-21, after deployment)\n\nMy [earlier comment in this issue](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4509010744) presented a 4-param diff (`EK3_SRC1_POSZ` plus three `EK3_GPS_OFFS_X/Y/Z` rows). That's wrong on the offset rows — **`EK3_GPS_OFFS_*` doesn't exist on this firmware**. MAVProxy returned `Unable to find parameter 'EK3_GPS_OFFS_X'` on the first attempt.\n\nArduPilot Rover consumes the GPS antenna lever-arm through `GPS_POS1_*` directly into the EKF; there is no separate `EK3_GPS_OFFS_*` family to set. `GPS_POS1_X/Y/Z` was already at `0.835 / 0.000 / -0.890` from the earlier #91 work, so no change there was needed today either.\n\n**The only substantive FCU change for #138 today was `EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 3`.** That landed cleanly; `param show` after the Cube reboot confirms `EK3_SRC1_POSZ 3.0` and the EKF boot sequence reports \"EKF3 IMU0/1/2 is using GPS\" — the visible confirmation of the change taking effect.\n\nBench-side validation passed all three Phase 1 criteria (see deployment dev log entry \"Block 2 sanity check\" timestamped 2026-05-21T12:16). #138's substantive deliverable is in place; in-water trackline validation moved to offline bag analysis as part of [#150 topic 1](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/150).\n\nOne caveat surfaced by gabby agent's in-water cross-check that's not yet diagnosed: a likely lever-arm double-count downstream in `mru_transform` / `sea_surface_estimator` (1.78 m systematic bias = 2 × |GPS_POS1_Z|, sign-flipped result is within 24 cm of the NOAA forecast). Held pending Roland's bag review before filing a fix-direction issue. So this issue's closure status is \"FCU side delivered; downstream lever-arm regression pending review\" rather than fully closed.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}